    "text": "<p>(a) According to principle of calorimetry,<br />heat gained <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;heat lost<br />Heat is lost by steam in two stages</p><p>(i) Change of state from steam at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> to water at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>540</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>(ii) To change water at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> to water at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is the mass of the steam condensed.</p><p>Total heat lost by steam is<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>540</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>540</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>560</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Heat gained by calorimeter and its contents is<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>80</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>65</mn><mtext>&#160;cal&#160;</mtext></math></p><p><math 